    {
        "content": "<p>dhil opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15110\">PR #15110</a> from <code>dhil:stack-switching-init-checks</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This patch adds some defense-in-depth measure to prevent the engine from segfaulting due to stack overflow on the initial entry to a high-arity continuation.</p>\n<p>The principal idea is to calculate the required headroom for the continuation's persistent control data. I have deliberately opted for a runtime calculation rather than compile-time calculation for simplicity and to keep the changes local to the stack-switching feature. In principle, the result could be attached as metadata to the compiled artifact.</p>\n<p>Resolves #13020.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
